43	- From the cellular presentation of filling systems, chord-slide relations and lexicographic reduction of intersections show that every oriented zero-filling system is congruent to a mapping-class translate of the standard system A, hence s=[A] generates St_g. [reason: Because [A]=0 in St_g, a reduction of every filling system to a G-translate of A cannot prove that St_g is cyclic on [A]; at best it reconfirms that degenerate or standard systems contribute the zero class, not a cyclic generator.]
44	- For every basis pure tensor t of odd degree r some symplectic plane H_i occurs oddly often, so τ_i t=−t; combined with [s⊗v]=[s⊗τ_i v] and s=[A] this forces all coinvariants of St_g⊗H_Q^{⊗r} to vanish, and therefore H^{4g-3}(G_{g,1};H_Q^{⊗r})=0 and H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{⊗5})=0. [reason: The half-turn coinvariance identity is applied to the zero class s=[A] in St_g, so the sign flip on odd tensors never sees a nontrivial Steinberg factor. The resulting vanishing of (St_g⊗H^{⊗5})_G and of H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{⊗5}) is not established by this argument.]
