- The weight floor gives W_{26}H^{25}(M_{6,5};Q(-1)^4)=0 and reduces W_{26}H^{25}(M_{6,5};R^1p_*Q) to a quotient of W_{26}H^{25}(M_{6,5};H), with kernel a subquotient of (W_{24}H^{24}(M_{6,5};Q)(-1))^4. [evidence: mechanical; For a pure coefficient system of weight w, H^p has weights at least p+w. Thus H^{25} with Q(-1) coefficients has weights at least 27, while H^{24} has weights at least 26; strictness of mixed Hodge structures applies to the coefficient long exact sequence.]
- For an effective divisor Gamma of degree 6, the f=4 obstruction vanishes, while the f=5 obstruction is nonzero exactly when O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to L=W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}. [evidence: mechanical; The two obstruction line bundles have degrees -4 and 0. A negative-degree line bundle has no section, and a degree-zero line bundle on a smooth connected projective curve has a nonzero section exactly when it is trivial.]
- The line bundle L=W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1} has degree 6 and satisfies chi(L)=1, hence h^0(L) is at least 1. [evidence: mechanical; Since deg(W_5)=16 and deg(omega_C)=10, deg(L)=6. Riemann-Roch gives chi(L)=6+1-6=1, so h^0(L)=1+h^1(L).]
- Over the reduced-support open of a relative degree-six linear system, ordering the six distinct support points gives a finite etale S_6-torsor. [evidence: mechanical; A reduced degree-six divisor has exactly 6! orderings, and the free permutation action is etale over the pairwise-distinct locus; the reduced-support condition is open.]
- For d=3g-3+n, the open input is W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}), identified by Poincare duality with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n})(d). [evidence: mechanical; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0001 (mechanically_verified; cases all).]
- For the forgetful map M_{6,6}->M_{6,5}, H^{26}(M_{6,5};Q) vanishes because 26 exceeds vcd(M_{6,5})=25; with fibre cohomology only in degrees 0 and 1, no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26. [evidence: mechanical; Packet adjudicated finding FND-0036 (mechanically_verified; degree 26, map M_{6,6} to M_{6,5}).]
- dim M_{6,6}=3*6-3+6=21. [evidence: mechanical; Standard dimension formula 3g-3+n evaluated at g=n=6 in the packet target and argument setup.]
- For g=n=6 and deg Gamma=6, chi(O_C(Gamma))=6-6+1=1, so any 2-term complex universally computing R pi_* O(Gamma) has ranks differing by 1. [evidence: mechanical; Riemann-Roch arithmetic chi=deg-g+1 visible in the Fitting/determinantal rank bookkeeping.]
- At g=n=6 the obstruction degrees are 4*4+6-12-14=-4 for f=4 and 4*5+6-12-14=0 for f=5. [evidence: mechanical; Direct substitution into the SRC-0004 formula deg=4f_i+n-2g-14.]
- At g=6 one has deg(W_4)=20 and deg(W_5)=16; for deg Γ=6, deg(ω_C⊗W_4^vee(Γ))=10-20+6=-4 and deg(ω_C⊗W_5^vee(Γ))=10-16+6=0. [evidence: mechanical; Direct arithmetic from deg(W_f)=4g+12-4f, deg(ω_C)=2g-2, and n=deg Γ=6]
- For L=W_5⊗ω_C^{-1} one has deg(L)=16-10=6; on a smooth genus-6 curve χ(L)=deg(L)-g+1=1, hence h^0(L)=1+h^1(L)≥1 and the full Abel–Jacobi fibre in Sym^6 is nonempty. [evidence: mechanical; Riemann–Roch arithmetic deg(L)=6 and χ(L)=6-6+1=1 imply h^0(L)≥χ(L)=1]
- For d=3g-3+n, the open input is W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n}), identified by Poincaré duality with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n})(d). [evidence: mechanical; C66-001-v3 adjudicated finding FND-0001 [mechanically_verified; cases: all]]
- For d=3g-3+n, the open input group is W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{g,n};Q), identified by Poincaré duality with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_{g,n};Q)(d). [evidence: mechanical; C66-001-v3 adjudicated finding FND-0001 [mechanically_verified; cases: all]]
- At g=6 the degree formula gives deg(W_5|_C) = 4*6+12-4*5 = 16 and deg(W_4|_C) = 4*6+12-4*4 = 20; with deg(omega_C) = 2g-2 = 10 the residual bundle L := W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1} has deg(L) = 16-10 = 6. [evidence: mechanical; Direct substitution into deg(W_f|_C)=4g+12-4f at g=6, f=5 and f=4; deg(L)=deg(W_5)-deg(omega_C)=16-10=6. Same numerics are recorded verbatim in the packet bullet 'deg(W_5)=16 and deg(W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1})=6 for g=6'.]
- At g=6, n=6 and for any effective degree-six divisor Gamma: deg(omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma)) = 4*5+6-12-14 = 0 and deg(omega_C tensor W_4^vee(Gamma)) = 4*4+6-12-14 = -4. [evidence: mechanical; Direct substitution into 4f+n-2g-14 with g=6, n=6: f=5 gives 20+6-12-14=0; f=4 gives 16+6-12-14=-4. Cross-checks against deg(omega_C)-deg(W_f)+n = 10-16+6=0 and 10-20+6=-4.]
