on": "", "kind": "working_context_constraint", "subject": "smoothness-from-dimension-count: 'Smoothness of the ordered reduced evaluation-failure locus as a 17-dimensional stack in M_{6,6} is deduced from the dimension count alone' is not used. The only smoothness asserted is that of AJ_B -> B, which follows from the Zariski-locally trivial projective-bundle structure; no smoothness, regularity or transversality statement is made about any locus in M_{6,6}."}, {"disposition": "", "kind": "working_context_constraint", "subject": "closed-pure-codim-4-gysin: 'Identify the balanced reduced-support relative linear system with a closed pure-codimension-4 subvariety Z in M_{6,6} and apply codimension-4 Gysin' is not used. No closedness in M_{6,6} is claimed, and no Gysin or cohomology-with-supports argument occurs."}, {"disposition": "", "kind": "working_context_constraint", "subject": "global-splitting-from-fibrewise-balanced: 'Infer a global splitting W = W_4 + W_5 over the universal balanced tetragonal base from the fibrewise balanced condition' is not used. Step 4d uses only the filtration 0 -> W_4 -> W -> W_5 -> 0 and the snake lemma, reproved fibrewise; the relative form is imported from ATT-0048 CLM-0048-3/CLM-0048-6, which are also splitting-free. The block-diagonal 12-by-12 minor factorisation is deliberately avoided."}, {"disposition": "", "kind": "working_context_constraint", "subject": "quantify-W5-or-L-over-the-family: 'Quantifying the obstruction splitting, W_5, or L over the whole family rather than over geometric fibres' is addressed rather than repeated: Step 6a notes that L is well defined only up to a Pic(B)-twist, and that both objects actually used -- the class a_L in the relative Picard Pic^6_{C_B/B} and the projectivisation P(p_*L_B) -- are invariant under that twist, so the P^2-bundle statement is canonical."}, {"disposition": "", "kind": "working_context_constraint", "subject": "expected-6-versus-actual-4-implies-nowhere-lci: 'From expected determi